{
  "_meta": {
    "canonical": "plan.md 7.2 -- ledger row fields; this is the type catalogue the generator draws from",
    "status": "DRAFT CAPABILITIES -- needs M4's review",
    "type_match": "An asset counts toward a requirement if and only if asset.quantity == requirement.quantity. plan.md 7.3 invariant 1 (type match) therefore falls out of the data and needs no separate code path.",
    "distractors": "quantity == null means the type contributes to NO requirement. These are real salvage assets that cannot satisfy the scalar -- the ledger must contain some, or V3 is passable by naming anything.",
    "frozen": true,
    "granularity_floor": "A lean arm (SCARCE 0.5x, INFEASIBLE 0.25x) and the OVERCOMMIT trap both need the requirement to be expressible in assets SMALLER than it. Whole-asset granularity means the smallest contributing capability_band floor must sit at or below 0.25 x the smallest requirement in requirements.json's `small` band, or build_scenario cannot place that cell in that arm and raises. workboat, pulling_winch_set and portable_pump exist for that reason: they are the small tier, not realism garnish. DRAFT magnitudes - need M4's review.",
    "eta_model": "ETA is derived, not drawn: eta_h = mobilise_h + distance_nm / speed_kn for an asset at a port, and UNDERWAY_SETUP_H + distance_nm / speed_kn for a floating asset already underway at sea. Each chain (one image's four arms) gets its own fictional ports at fixed distances (geography below), so two assets at the same port differ in ETA only by type speed and mobilisation. Replaces the per-type eta_band_h, under which location carried no information about arrival (docs/corpus_realism.md sec. 1). Non-floating kit moves at the speed of whatever carries it: lift bags travel as deck cargo on a dive-support vessel (10 kn), not by road. DRAFT speeds and mobilisation times - need M4's review.",
    "prefix": "Ledger IDs are <prefix>-<NNN>, the prefix fixed per type so a workboat is not a TUG. Numbers are drawn without replacement from 1..ID_NUMBER_MAX per prefix on the SURPLUS ledger and kept by every arm that contains the asset (nested arms), so gaps in the numbering carry no information about the arm."
  },
